    <item>
      <title>Researchers say COVID-19 could have been in U.S. back in December 2019 based on data</title>
      <link>https://cwbaltimore.com/news/researchers-say-covid-19-could-have-been-in-us-back-in-december-2019-based-on-data-coronavirus-china-wuhan-united-states</link>
      <description>NASHVILLE, Tenn. (WZTV) — New research from doctors at UCLA's David Geffen School of Medicine and the UW School of Public Health in Seattle estimates SARS-CoV-2 could have been in the United States as far back as December. The researchers examined U. S. health system data representing 2. 5 million patient visits each year from July 2014 to February 29, 2020. They then examined the number of excess hospital visits and clinic visits last winter and compared it to previous seasons.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://cwbaltimore.com/news/researchers-say-covid-19-could-have-been-in-us-back-in-december-2019-based-on-data-coronavirus-china-wuhan-united-states</guid>
